**Summary of implementation (prd004-ts R1-R5):**

- **cmd/ts/main.go**: Reads stdin line-by-line via `bufio.NewReader`, prepends timestamps formatted via strftime→Go layout conversion. Supports `-s` (elapsed since start), `-i` (incremental per-line), and `-m` (monotonic, no-op in Go since `time.Sub()` uses monotonic readings automatically). Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` per shared protocol. Handles partial lines without adding extra newlines.

- **cmd/ts/ts_test.go**: 9 differential test cases (default format, empty stdin, partial line, custom format, -s, -i, -m, TZ env, -m with -s) using `testutils.TimestampNormalizer` for wall-clock masking. Graceful skip via `exec.LookPath("ts")`. Standalone `TestInvalidFlag` for error case where Go/Perl error formats differ.